cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use docrot or its published dataset, please cite it as follows:"
title: "docrot: measuring documentation image rot in public Git repositories"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aurora"
    email: "aurora@codebyaurora.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/auroraxo/docrot"
url: "https://codebyaurora.com/docrot/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - documentation
  - link-rot
  - image-rot
  - repository-mining
  - open-source
abstract: >-
  docrot reads the Markdown of a repository at a named commit, resolves every
  image reference, and reports which images no longer load and which hosts
  must stay online for them to keep loading. The published corpus covers the
  300 most-used repositories with a commit-pinned, regression-gated dataset
  and an interactive report.
